course: dictionary
lesson: 451
title: Arguers and reasons
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An arguer is a person who argues. The word can mean two things: someone who quarrels a lot, or someone who gives reasons for an opinion. It is a rare word, so you will mostly meet it in debates, where a «good arguer» makes a strong case. Look at the words around it: strong, case and reasons are your clues.
explain: «Strong arguers steelman: they say the other idea back in its best, strongest words before answering it, and they look for common ground, what both sides want.» Steelman is a word the writer uses here. The clues show it means saying someone else's idea in its best, fairest form before you answer it. Common ground is what both sides agree they want.
explain: Everyday talk usually says «debater» or «argues a lot» instead of arguer. So when you read arguer, ask yourself: is this person quarrelling, or giving reasons? The sentence will tell you which one.
fact: An arguer is a person who argues.
fact: An arguer can be someone who quarrels a lot, or someone who gives reasons for an opinion.
fact: In a debate, a good arguer makes a strong case with clear reasons.
fact: To steelman means to say another person's idea back in its best, strongest words before you answer it.
fact: Common ground means what both sides agree on or want.
exercise: «Strong arguers steelman: they say the other idea back in its best, strongest words before answering it.» What do strong arguers do first? | *Say the other idea back in its best words | Shout until the other person stops | Agree with everything at once | Ignore the other idea completely
exercise: In a debate, what does a good arguer do? | Only asks questions about the weather | Quarrels loudly and wins by shouting | *Makes a strong case with clear reasons | Says nothing at all
exercise: Which everyday word could replace arguer in «She is a good arguer»? | Painter | Sleeper | Gardener | *Debater
test: «Strong arguers steelman...» What does steelman mean here? | *Saying the other idea back in its best, strongest words | Shouting over the other person | Forgetting the other idea | Saying the other idea back in its weakest words
test: What can an arguer be? | A large building | A person who only paints pictures | *A person who quarrels a lot or gives reasons for an opinion | A kind of fast animal
exam: Lena says, «A good arguer wins by shouting.» Is Lena right? | Yes, if the other person is quiet | No, arguers never speak | Yes, shouting always wins | *No, a good arguer gives clear reasons and looks for common ground
